, \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1795153764620899001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b324bc78-6b12-452d-aa60-332c01bd309b","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"8aa0-2120-5ef3-4750"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nDiscovered while triaging breezy-hogged-mastiff, which owns `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/unclassified.args`. These 13 entries move to `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/detached-maintenance.args`, which this bug owns.\n\n`compact_trigger.maybe_compact` (`src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py:374`) and `gc_trigger.maybe_gc` (`src/rebar/_snapshot/gc_trigger.py:180`) return at once on `sys.platform == \"win32\"`. The docstring gives the reason as the store lock's `fcntl` import crashing a detached child, but the lock kernel now has a Windows leg (`src/rebar/_store/lock_kernel.py`, commit `035b7371de8`). The tests expect the trigger to fold inline or spawn a sweep and get no call (`assert []`, `0 == 1`).\n\nEvidence: Windows runs on throwaway branch `tmp/w05-remeasure` with origin/main `717c50f8b33` code plus a selection-only workflow change: run 44665461131 (the 242 `unclassified.args` entries; 48 passed, 194 failed or errored) and run 44681457334 (the 194, xdist, JUnit XML with full tracebacks). Both 2026-11-19 PST.\n\nModules:\n- `tests/unit/test_compact_trigger.py` (8)\n- `tests/unit/test_snapshot_gc_trigger.py` (5)\n\n## Approach\nRe-establish whether the detached sweep and GC can run on Windows now that the lock kernel is portable. Enable them and keep the tests, or mark the tests Windows-skipped with the reason. Either way the lines leave `detached-maintenance.args`.\n\n## Scope\nTest or product code for the listed modules, plus `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/detached-maintenance.args` (remove each fixed line; delete the file and its `@` reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml` once empty).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every line removed from `detached-maintenance.args` names a test that passed in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `detached-maintenance.args` is empty and deleted with its reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml`, or each remaining line names a test recorded on this ticket as intentionally unsupported on Windows with the reason.\n","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":".github/windows-sweep-deselect/detached-maintenance.args","reason":"remove each line as its test is fixed"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["windows","portability"],"ticket_id":"41e5-5e7c-52f5-43c6","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep: out-of-band compaction and snapshot GC are a no-op on Windows, so 13 trigger tests see no spawn","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["9e4936b5-b875-4c25-b96c-963ad9c066ea","b324bc78-6b12-452d-aa60-332c01bd309b","aae555a1-bcf3-4489-89a8-2ac1208d3a89"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795153822547387002,"uuid":"491ec8c2-28db-4a4c-9042-ba27729bc6e3"}